{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens","id":1527897,"title":"Extraordinary Citizens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-03T20:40:50-08:00","id":1527897,"title":"Extraordinary Citizens","content":"I am trying to get a sense about what it's like to be an Extraordinary Citizen (the Technocracy's answer to Sleeper Sorcerers). Like, is it possible to be an Extraordinary Citizen through being a lone practitioner like many Sorcerers? I can totally see a Chemist or Chemical Engineer becoming an alchemist without knowing that is what they have become. Also, aren't most of the Paths rebranded for Extraordinary Citizens? I can't imagine an EC who practices, say, Summoning actually calling it &quot;Summoning.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26676-squiggles","name":"Squiggles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26676_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T21:54:26-08:00","id":1527901,"title":"","content":"Yes, different sorcerers have different names for the Paths; and the names used by techno-sorcerers are (almost?) always technological in nature. <b>Sorcerer Revised</b> went so far as to point out that sorcerers with an earthier feel often called Alchemy \u201cHerbalism\u201d, while tech-oriented sorcerers prefer to call it \u201cAdvanced Chemistry\u201d. Note that a chemist wouldn't become an Alchemist; he'd unlock the secrets of Advanced Chemistry. <br /> <br /> In a similar way, I could see Extraordinary Citizens referring to Enchantment as Fabrication, Healing as Advanced Medicine, Quintessence Manipulation as Advanced Economics, Gauntlet Manipulation as Dimensional Control, Hellfire as Energetics, and so on. Other Paths have perfectly fine names (such as Conveyance, Fascination, and Fortune); you don't have to change <i>everything. </i><br /> <br /> And finally, note that the Union is far more likely to forge new Paths than the Traditions are. So by all rights, there ought to be a number of Paths out there designed specifically for Extraordinary Citizens. The trick is in finding something that the existing Paths don't already cover, that Extraordinary Citizens might find useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-03T22:40:25-08:00","id":1527905,"title":"","content":"I suspect that lone practitioners of Advanced Science are akin to lone (and eccentric) geniuses, possibly even seen as potential dangers by the Technocracy, as they haven't undergone all the proper vetting, orientation, and training (ie indoctrination) to be classified as an &quot;Extraordinary <i>Citizen</i>&quot; of the Union. (That second word is key.)<br /> <br /> This is especially true for anyone pursuing things like Advanced Dimensional Science, Advanced Social Influence, or Advanced Combat Studies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T00:27:45-08:00","id":1527909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1527901#post1527901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, note that the Union is far more likely to forge new Paths than the Traditions are. So by all rights, there ought to be a number of Paths out there designed specifically for Extraordinary Citizens. The trick is in finding something that the existing Paths don't already cover, that Extraordinary Citizens might find useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>For this one, M20 Sorcerer has a sidebar on Page 16 that mentions the pipeline of new the Technocracy creating new paths (Going from Enlightened Scientist, to Enlightened Citizen studying the path and then implying that these paths get added to the consensus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Amusingly, this might mean that there might have been a 'Path of Cellphone' at one point .: 0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T00:49:58-08:00","id":1527911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1527901#post1527901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, note that the Union is far more likely to forge new Paths than the Traditions are. So by all rights, there ought to be a number of Paths out there designed specifically for Extraordinary Citizens. The trick is in finding something that the existing Paths don't already cover, that Extraordinary Citizens might find useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite a few that fit into that category made it into psychic phenomena instead; notably there was no official Technomancy Path until Sorcerer 20, and then it's a weird Necromancy/Technomancy mix. I guess Psychics work thematically quite well as ECs, but a few more Sorcery Paths that play on Advanced Science would be nice to have.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T00:50:54-08:00","id":1527912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Furoan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1527909#post1527909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For this one, M20 Sorcerer has a sidebar on Page 16 that mentions the pipeline of new the Technocracy creating new paths (Going from Enlightened Scientist, to Enlightened Citizen studying the path and then implying that these paths get added to the consensus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Amusingly, this might mean that there might have been a 'Path of Cellphone' at one point .: 0</div> </div> </div> </div>And for what it's worth, Sorcerer: Paths of Power has a more detailed examination of that process.<br /> <br /> That said, I think that what both of those books present makes it too easy for a mage to create a new Path; instead, I'd treat the process as a variation or application of Terranorming as described in the Operative's Dossier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-04-2024, 03:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-04T00:59:37-08:00","id":1527913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1527911#post1527911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a few that fit into that category made it into psychic phenomena instead; notably there was no official Technomancy Path until Sorcerer 20, and then it's a weird Necromancy/Technomancy mix. I guess Psychics work thematically quite well as ECs, but a few more Sorcery Paths that play on Advanced Science would be nice to have.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The new Paths and Psychic Phenomena found in <b>M20 Sorcerer</b> originated in <b>Ghost Hunters</b>, which is why they're so closely associated with necromancy. <br /> <br /> Also note that the section about Mages and New Paths doesn't technically say anything about creating new Psychic Phenomena; though I can see the argument for why one would allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T11:08:36-08:00","id":1528040,"title":"","content":"I've never had an EC Sorcerer player or played one myself, so this thread got me thinking about what would go into chargen for one. 'Soft' science based characters who employ Social Engineering (Fascination) or Market Manipulation (Fortune, Divination) don't seem to deviate too much from the 'standard', but for 'hard' sciences like physics and chemistry I think there are some mechanical restrictions.<br /> <br /> For one, if your Focus depends on working through the veneer of mundane causality, most EC Sorcerers likely do not cast ad-hoc spells and would have the Ritual Sleeper flaw. You need your equipment and laboratory to stay in your Focus. Or at least an Instrument that serves as a proxy for your powers. There's the Psi Focus flaw that does that for psychic powers, but I don't recall if there was a similar flaw that makes an Instrument mandatory for casting sorcery.<br /> <br /> Also, you probably want to create Trinkets, Gadgets, or Devices to get any practical utility out of your Rituals/Spells. Your quantum-phase-refluxor isn't much fun if it is not portable to reproduce the effect outside of the laboratory. So Enchanting is probably on top of the list of powers to get - luckily, it is pretty versatile in the effects it can produce. This falls flat for anything Biology though, and depending on the specific field would likely need importing some Paths and Rituals from elsewhere (blood sorcery) or creating new ones. Making an EC geneticist would require some leg-work.<br /> <br /> There are probably a number of scientific disciplines I haven't considered yet which would be difficult to make into an interesting Path. Concept-wise abstract things like Mathemancy sound like fun but I'm not sure you would get good gameplay out of it. Maybe there is way to make a generic Science Path work that uses Aspects to enhance mundane effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T11:34:47-08:00","id":1528042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1528040#post1528040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never had an EC Sorcerer player or played one myself, so this thread got me thinking about what would go into chargen for one. 'Soft' science based characters who employ Social Engineering (Fascination) or Market Manipulation (Fortune, Divination) don't seem to deviate too much from the 'standard', but for 'hard' sciences like physics and chemistry I think there are some mechanical restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Quintessence Manipulation for the soft sciences, in the form of money magic. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1528040#post1528040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one, if your Focus depends on working through the veneer of mundane causality, most EC Sorcerers likely do not cast ad-hoc spells and would have the Ritual Sleeper flaw. You need your equipment and laboratory to stay in your Focus. Or at least an Instrument that serves as a proxy for your powers. There's the Psi Focus flaw that does that for psychic powers, but I don't recall if there was a similar flaw that makes an Instrument mandatory for casting sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's inherent to sorcery: they don't have the option to Work Without Focus or to grow beyond their tools, so the use of Instruments is mandatory. <br /> <br /> Note that this means that Hellfire is quite usable by a techno-sorcerer, as long as he's equipped with a blaster and isn't in a situation with observers (who tend to make sorcery fail). Ritual Sleeper is <i>not</i> a requirement. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1528040#post1528040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you probably want to create Trinkets, Gadgets, or Devices to get any practical utility out of your Rituals/Spells. Your quantum-phase-refluxor isn't much fun if it is not portable to reproduce the effect outside of the laboratory. So Enchanting is probably on top of the list of powers to get - luckily, it is pretty versatile in the effects it can produce. This falls flat for anything Biology though, and depending on the specific field would likely need importing some Paths and Rituals from elsewhere (blood sorcery) or creating new ones. Making an EC geneticist would require some leg-work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alchemy covers a lot of ground there (Herbalism got folded into it); and you might develop a variant of Enchantment that produces magical creatures, assuming Enchantment can't do that already: it's the Path I'd use for creating bionic limbs or cybernetic implants. In that regard, Task Force Zero from <b>Demon Hunter X</b> might be worth looking at for some inspiration in that regard. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1527897-extraordinary-citizens?p=1528040#post1528040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are probably a number of scientific disciplines I haven't considered yet which would be difficult to make into an interesting Path. Concept-wise abstract things like Mathemancy sound like fun but I'm not sure you would get good gameplay out of it. Maybe there is way to make a generic Science Path work that uses Aspects to enhance mundane effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Strength of Psyche Merit lets you expend Quintessence to ease the difficulty on mental tasks. Also, Technopathy could be reworked as a Path to give you something for the formal science of information technology. But in general, there's not much I can think of that would work for the formal sciences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T12:13:34-08:00","id":1528044,"title":"","content":"Addendum (because these days, editing a post is a good way to make it get suspended for Moderator approval): while Mathematics as a whole isn't going to be the basis for a single Path, I could see a Geometry Path that's founded on the Correspondence Sphere. It generally wouldn't be the sort of thing that you'd practice in Times Square; but there's nothing saying that techno-sorcery can't be Hypertech. And I could definitely see the Extraordinary Citizens among the Void Engineers getting into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T18:25:26-08:00","id":1528072,"title":"","content":"Random musings:<br /> <br /> Advanced Chemistry (Alchemy &amp; Herbalism)<br /> Advanced Transportation (Conveyance, maybe also Conjuration)<br /> Advanced Patronage (Cursing/Fortune)<br /> Advanced Investigation (Divination)<br /> Advanced Engineering (Enchantment)<br /> Advanced Marketing/Social Engineering (Fascination)<br /> Advanced Medicine (Healing)<br /> Advanced Thermodynamics (Hellfire)<br /> Advanced Oneirology (Oneiromancy) <br /> Advanced Biomanipulation (Shapeshifting) <br /> Advanced Extradimensional Studies (Summoning/Binding/Warding &amp; Ephemera &amp; Spirit Chasing) <br /> Advanced Meteorology (Weather Control)<br /> <br /> Mana Manipulation and Shadowcasting are the only two pre-Sorcerer20 ones I can't think of counterparts for. <br /> <br /> Also, Advanced Combat Studies, for the theoretical/unpublished Path of War that was meant to supersede that terrible Knife Fighting power in WoD: [The Rom] and allow for Akashic Sorcerers do perform superhuman Do/martial arts abilities, as well as handling things like Red Spear spirit warriors, Etheric superhumans, Thanatoic assassins, Hermetic fencing masters, and Syndicate Enforcers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T18:40:36-08:00","id":1528075,"title":"","content":"Shadows are an absence of energy. Maybe Advanced Energy Manipulation?<br /> <br /> In fact something like Advanced Energetic Engineering might cover both Shadows and Mana Manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-05T19:08:37-08:00","id":1528077,"title":"","content":"Advanced Quantum Theory for Mana Manipulation maybe? \ud83e\udd14<br /> <br /> Also musing on most likely training/pursuits: <br /> <br /> NWO: Investigation, Social Engineering, Oneirology, Combat Studies<br /> Iteration X: Chemistry, Transportation, Engineering, Medicine, Thermodynamics, Meteorology<br /> Progenitors: Chemistry, Medicine, Oneirology, Biomanipulation<br /> Syndicate: Patronage, Investigation, Marketing, Combat Studies<br /> Void Engineers: Transportation, Engineering, Thermodynamics, Oneirology, Extradimensional Studies<br /> <br /> Virtual Adepts: Investigation, Engineering, Social Engineering, Oneirology, Combat Studies (probably also a specialized version of Astral Projection that works only for the Digital Web)<br /> <br /> Etherites would likely replace Advanced with Etheric, and maybe have slightly archaic names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-06T07:23:28-08:00","id":1528103,"title":"","content":"Mana Manipulation isn't in M20 Sorcerer; Quintessence Manipulation replaces it. And with that change, it becomes entirely possible to approach that Path the same way that the Syndicate approaches Prime, through a theory of hypereconomic utility. And that is exactly how I'd expect a techno-sorcerer in the Syndicate (or any other faction that practices Hypereconomics) to view Quintessence Manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}